    "lawCode": "Add §170-d, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7350\n\nSPONSOR: KAPLAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the executive law, in relation to directing empire state\ndevelopment to publish and maintain a list of available programs to\nassist small businesses\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis legislation would require ESDC to coordinate with the State Agen-\ncies and State Authorities to collect information on programs offered by\neach agency and authority that assist small business. This information\nonce collected is to be organized and shared on the ESDC website.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 adds a new section 170-c to the Executive Law to require ESDC\nin cooperation with every state agency and authority to develop and\nmaintain a list of programs offered.  This section defines small busi-\nness meaning fifty or fewer employees.  Specifically within 180 days of\nthe effective date and annually thereafter, state agencies and authori-\nties shall provide to ESDC a list of programs assisting small business,\nincluding a brief description along with contact information for the\nprogram.\n\nWithin 270 days of the effective date and annually thereafter, ESDC\nshall compile a list of all programs including a description of each\nprogram and contact information for each program as provided to them,\nand shall make this information on their website in a clear and conspic-\nuous location.\n\nSection 2 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nNew York offers numerous programs across a variety of agencies and\nauthorities that are helpful to small business. However, there is no\nclearinghouse where a small business can easily find various programs\nfrom different agencies. This legislation requires conversation between\nESDC and the other entities to work collectively to collect and make\nthis information more readily available. This common sense legislation\nseeks to help New York State tout the amazing programs it has to offer\nwhile assisting small business take advantage of the amazing and numer-\nous programs and benefits New York has to offer.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nMinimal.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
