  "chapter": 339,
  "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
  "text": "\n \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 44 Chapter 339\n \n        MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 7350, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the executive law, in relation to directing empire\n        state development to publish and maintain a  list  of  available\n        programs to assist small businesses\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This  bill  amends  provisions  of  the Executive Law to require state\nagencies and authorities to annually provide  empire  state  development\nwith  their  program offerings to assist small businesses for display on\nthe empire state development website.\n \n  I have secured an agreement with the Legislature to make certain tech-\nnical changes to the  bill.  The  changes  would  include  amending  the\nEconomic  Development  Law  rather than the Executive Law, the effective\ndate to mid-year 2021, and directing state agencies and  authorities  to\nprovide  the required information to the department of economic develop-\nment by business size, business type, or ownership  requirements.    The\ndepartment  of  economic  development  is  then  required to display the\nsupplied information in the same manner. On the basis of this agreement,\nI am pleased to sign this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                      (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2020
 },
